ilds. If so, this test might fail and…"],["90cb6c52_8bdd018a",47,-21,1,"Shouldn't this be removed as well together with the declaration in `media_switches.h`?"],["9af0893f_38c3b18b",48,-21,1,"I would retain this for now: I'm not sure if this code is reachable when `BUILDFLAG(IS_CASTOS)` is true, but if it is, we don't want to use `VideoDecoderType::kOutOfProcess`."],["afd9a718_55eace19",46,-21,1,"nit: Jonathan requested in an earlier patchset that this blank line be kept."],["28e360f0_5ba7ca6d",46,-17,1,"This seems unintended"],["4d1ecd05_dfcae048",49,-17,1,"nit: It seems like this can be removed as well since the comment references a feature flag that no longer exists."],["56340717_4ae95b69",47,-17,1,"nit: This empty `#if...#endif` block is no longer needed."],["bc768a50_b59e3b33",47,-16,1,"What seems simplest is to replace this buildflag to be ENABLE_OOP_VIDEO_DECODER and have it only true iff is_chromeos = true in media_options.gni. Then this entire function can be removed, and the…"],["d391922f_f78169cb",47,-16,1,"This can likely be closed as WontFix and this use if IS_CASTOS removed, but I CCed the reporter to confirm."],["d1108799_8ffe4256",44,-10,1,"Remove flag?"],["0826d3b8_08e851b8",50,-9,1,"Does this ever occur now? I think it's only true for ChromeOS?"],["092c158c_25292129",51,-9,1,"We're not going to do this, so we should replace all of these buildflags with `enable_oop_video_decoder`"],["603e8f58_c4222468",52,-9,1,"Nit: Use &&"],["8799989b_580aab45",47,-9,1,"Looks like you still have the function?"],["a6901ee0_df8f8189",47,-9,1,"The function should be removed too now."],["de2c0d39_b3afc6cf",53,-9,1,"Since ENABLE_OOP_VIDEO_DECODER requires USE_LINUX_VIDEO_ACCELERATION, I think the second clause can be removed."],["cc6993e8_24f58b70",54,-7,1,"This should go below non-buildflag includes like the section starting at l.42"],["128580d6_643d3bf2",3,-1,1,"update the commit message here... there is a rename of a build flag as well, it's not just removing a flag? I suppose it's not possible to put the rename of the build flag in one CL then remove the…"],["65a972b6_d6079cc3",55,-1,0,"does this comment need updating?"],["6d0ec0af_663b8e2f",51,-1,0,"have you confirmed there are no bots (e.g. FYI bots) that specify this whose configuration might need to be updated because this build flag has changed?"],["f43a34f2_7b7e2b01",56,-1,0,"do we need to actually enable this explicitly if the name is the same? what effect does this have?"]],0,148],[8384338,20707,171,4.195,3.394,[[2,0.93,137,161],[6,0.048,6,8],[5,0.011,7,1],[3,0.011,88,1]],[],0,149],[8380882,20707,149,4.195,3.394,[[2,138]],[],0,150],[8390538,20707,100,2.344,1.853,[[2,139]],[],0,151],[8389197,20708,90,2.344,1.853,[[2,0.907,140,83],[3,0.072,89,6],[17,0.021,4,1]],[],0,152],[8390798,20708,117,2.344,1.853,[[2,0.969,141,115],[65,0.016,0,1],[7,0.016,2,1]],[],0,153],[8393363,20708,273,7.579,6.176,[[2,0.958,142,264],[66,0.021,0,5],[3,0.014,90,3],[12,0.007,4,1]],[],0,154],[8404730,20711,99,2.344,1.853,[[2,143]],[],0,155],[8405646,20711,162,4.195,3.394,[[2,144]],[],0,156],[8402350,20711,153,4.195,3.394,[[2,0.987,145,152],[3,0.013,91,1]],[],0,157],[8402336,20711,124,2.344,1.853,[[2,0.984,146,123],[3,0.016,92,1]],[],0,158],[8402351,20711,144,4.195,3.394,[[2,0.98,147,142],[3,0.02,93,2]],[],0,159],[8411666,20712,130,4.195,3.394,[[2,0.985,148,129],[3,0.015,94,1]],[],0,160],[8413310,20712,97,2.344,1.853,[[2,0.931,149,91],[3,0.069,95,6]],[["6a17eb03_e6d7c6cb",4,0,1,"QQ - one of the main reasons to do the regular `file` / `file_impl` build target split is to have it such that only the impl has the circular includes. If we end up doing things like this I believe…"]],0,161],[8416171,20712,286,7.579,6.176,[[2,0.875,150,264],[5,0.059,8,10],[3,0.016,96,4],[6,0.013,7,2],[67,0.006,0,1],[33,0.006,3,1],[29,0.006,1,1],[68,0.006,0,1],[10,0.006,2,1],[39,0.006,1,1]],[],0,162],[8410733,20712,179,4.195,3.394,[[2,0.978,151,176],[3,0.022,97,3]],[],0,163],[8414467,20712,208,4.195,3.394,[[2,0.776,152,173],[